Detailed readiness checklist and roadmap for deploying and operating the full AI Underwriter Platform (all code sets 3–5 combined). 

This is structured by phases: Pre-Deployment, Deployment, Post-Deployment / Operations, and Continuous Improvement.


---

1. Pre-Deployment Readiness Checklist

Infrastructure

[ ] Kubernetes cluster or VM provisioning completed (CPU, GPU for LLM inference).

[ ] Storage configured: S3 bucket / object storage for document uploads.

[ ] Redis cluster deployed and tested.

[ ] PostgreSQL / AsyncPG-compatible DB deployed and accessible.

[ ] Vault deployed and secrets paths configured (pii/db, pii/jwt).

[ ] Networking and firewall rules allow API, LLM, Redis, DB, and Vault connectivity.


Configuration

[ ] .env or ConfigMaps/Secrets populated with production values.

[ ] JWT secret and Fernet key generated and validated.

[ ] API keys generated for ingestion endpoints.

[ ] Prometheus and Grafana endpoints configured.

[ ] LLM endpoints (local or remote) validated for connectivity.


Code / Application

[ ] All code sets pulled and versioned:

Code Set 3: Policy LLM (SLOs, alerting, PrometheusRules, RemediationPlans).

Code Set 4: PII Deletion API + Worker.

Code Set 5: Enterprise API ingestion service.


[ ] Dependencies installed and tested in a virtual environment or container.

[ ] Docker images built for each service with health endpoints exposed.

[ ] Static code analysis, security scanning, and linting completed.


Observability

[ ] Prometheus rules loaded and tested.

[ ] Grafana dashboards deployed for:

LLM TPOT latency

Error budget (fast/slow)

Queue growth & GPU utilization

Worker success/failure/DLQ


[ ] Sentry or equivalent error tracking configured.



---

2. Deployment Roadmap

Phase 1: Core Services

[ ] Deploy Redis and DB. Verify connectivity from local environment.

[ ] Deploy Vault and verify secrets are retrievable with retries.

[ ] Deploy Enterprise API (Code Set 5).

[ ] Run smoke tests for:

API auth (API key + JWT)

Rate limiting

PDF malware scan & S3 upload



Phase 2: LLM Service

[ ] Deploy Policy LLM service (Code Set 3).

[ ] Load PrometheusRules & RemediationPlans.

[ ] Verify:

TPOT P95 latency reporting

Error rate metrics

GPU/queue saturation metrics


[ ] Run test requests to validate SLOs and alert triggering.


Phase 3: PII Deletion Worker

[ ] Deploy PII worker (Code Set 4).

[ ] Validate transactional deletion and audit hashing.

[ ] Test retry logic and DLQ functionality.

[ ] Ensure optional Fernet encryption is applied and verifiable.


Phase 4: Integration & End-to-End

[ ] Submit test applicant via ingestion API.

[ ] Validate flow:

1. API ingestion → Redis stream


2. LLM inference → risk scoring


3. PII deletion queue → audit log



[ ] Verify metrics: request counters, latency, LLM call success, DLQ counts.

[ ] Simulate edge cases: invalid JWT, malicious PDFs, rate limits.



---

3. Post-Deployment / Operations Checklist

Monitoring

[ ] Prometheus metrics streaming correctly.

[ ] Grafana dashboards reflecting live metrics.

[ ] Alerts and remediation plans tested (scaling, failover, security).

[ ] Sentry capturing unhandled exceptions.


Security

[ ] JWT and API keys rotated regularly.

[ ] Vault secrets rotation enabled.

[ ] Encrypted storage verified for PII.

[ ] PDF malware detection functional.


Resilience & Recovery

[ ] DLQ handling and retries tested.

[ ] Backoff and failover mechanisms validated.

[ ] Disaster recovery procedures documented for DB, Redis, S3, Vault.



---

4. Continuous Improvement Roadmap

Quarter	Focus	Tasks

Q1	Observability & SLO tuning	Adjust error budgets, latency thresholds, Grafana panels; optimize Prometheus rules.
Q2	LLM Model Updates	Upgrade or retrain local LLM, validate inference latency, ensure compatibility with API.
Q3	PII Compliance	Introduce automated compliance checks, audit reporting, encrypted backups.
Q4	Scale & Automation	Auto-scale LLM pods based on queue/GPU; enhance automated remediation plans.



---

5. Readiness Sign-Off Criteria

All components deployable via IaC or Helm/Manifests.

End-to-end API request completes successfully with correct risk scoring.

All metrics and dashboards operational.

Alerts trigger expected remediation plans.

PII deletion is transactional, auditable, and optionally encrypted.

Security, rate limiting, and JWT/API key validation verified.



---

Phase / Quarter       Milestones / Tasks                                QA / Gate
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Phase 0: Preparation  (Weeks 1-2)
----------------------
- Provision infrastructure: K8s, GPU nodes, Redis, DB
- Vault deployed & secrets configured
- Storage (S3) configured
- Environment variables & config validated
- Code sets pulled & Docker images built
QA Gate: Infrastructure & config verified, secrets retrieval tested

Phase 1: Core Services Deployment (Weeks 3-4)
---------------------------------------------
- Deploy Enterprise API (Code Set 5)
- Redis & DB connections validated
- JWT + API Key authentication tested
- Rate limiting functional
- Basic ingestion and S3 upload validated
QA Gate: Smoke test success, metrics visible, logs validated

Phase 2: LLM Service Deployment (Weeks 5-6)
--------------------------------------------
- Deploy Policy LLM service (Code Set 3)
- PrometheusRules & RemediationPlans loaded
- TPOT latency, error rate, GPU utilization metrics validated
- Test LLM inference requests and alert triggers
QA Gate: LLM responds correctly, SLO metrics accurate, alerts fire as expected

Phase 3: PII Deletion Worker Deployment (Weeks 7-8)
----------------------------------------------------
- Deploy PII worker (Code Set 4)
- Transactional deletion & audit hash verified
- Retry and DLQ handling tested
- Optional Fernet encryption validated
QA Gate: PII deletion end-to-end tested, DLQ entries triggered for failures

Phase 4: Integration & End-to-End Testing (Weeks 9-10)
------------------------------------------------------
- Submit test applicant via ingestion API
- Validate: API → Redis → LLM → Risk scoring → PII deletion
- Metrics verified: request counts, latency, LLM calls, DLQ counts
- Edge cases tested: invalid JWT, malicious PDFs, rate limits
QA Gate: Successful end-to-end workflow, metrics & logs validated, error handling verified

Phase 5: Production Readiness & Operations Handoff (Week 11)
------------------------------------------------------------
- Monitoring dashboards (Grafana) finalized
- Alerts & remediation plans fully operational
- Security audit: API keys, JWT, Vault secrets rotation
- Backup & disaster recovery validated
QA Gate: Ops team sign-off, production runbook completed

Continuous Improvement (Ongoing)
---------------------------------
- Quarterly review of SLOs, LLM model updates, scaling & automation
- Enhancements in PII compliance and audit
- Metrics & dashboards refinement
- Disaster recovery drills
QA Gate: Quarterly audit report, metrics & SLOs meet targets